        <p class="profile-detail-region">City · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kraków</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 700 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Around the 8th century, as a fortified settlement of the Vistulans, a Lechitic tribe; a legend attributes the founding to the mythical ruler Krakus.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> river in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesser-poland">Lesser Poland</a> region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, about 219 metres above sea level, at the meeting of the Kraków-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czestochowa">Częstochowa</a> Upland, the Małopolska Upland, the Sandomierz Basin and the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wawel-hill">Wawel Hill</a> with its castle and cathedral; the seat of the Piast and Jagiellonian kings; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-university">Jagiellonian University</a> of 1364; the Main Market Square and St Mary's Basilica; the Jewish quarter of Kazimierz; the Kraków Ghetto; Karol Wojtyła, who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-paul-ii">Pope John Paul II</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Kraków is the second-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesser-poland">Lesser Poland</a> Voivodeship, and its Old Town is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
